# Ubuntu 
* sudo apt update (refresh registry for update)
* sudo apt install -y postgresql postgresql-client postgresql-contrib (install pgsql, client and needed packages)
* psql --version (validate installation)
* pg_lsclusters (pg_cluster tooling. note port:5432 and data dir:/var/lib/postgresql/14/main/)
* dpkg -l | grep postgresql (checking all packages installed for pgsql)
* systemctl status postgresql@14-main.service (checking server status )
* sudo -iu postgres psql 
* postgres=# SELECT current_user, current_database(); 
* postgres=# SHOW config_file; 
* postgres=# SHOW hba_file; 
* postgres=# SHOW data_directory;
* postgres=# \conninfo 